    "text": "In figure, the optical fiber is <math><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long and has a diameter of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If a ray of light is incident on one end of the fiber at angle <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> , the number of reflections it makes before emerging from the other end is close to:<br />(refractive index of fiber is <math><mn>1.31</mn></math> , <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>40</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0.64</mn></math> and <math><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mn>0.49</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> .)<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c02eca14-3d8a-45f4-8ba5-83c423e736aa-image.png\" />",
    "image": null
  },
